11
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Clerks is a 1994 American black-and-white comedy film
written and directed by Kevin Smith.

12
00:50:10,909 --> 00:50:16,909
The film stars Brian O'Halloran, Jeff Anderson, Marilyn Ghigliotti, Jason Mewes, and Lisa Spoonauer, it presents a day in the
lives of store clerks Dante Hicks (O'Halloran) and Randal Graves (Anderson) as well as their acquaintances.

13
00:54:21,818 --> 00:54:27,818
It is the first of Smith's View Askewniverse films, and introduces several recurring
characters, notably Jay and Silent Bob (played by Mewes and Smith respectively).

14
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
The film was initially shot for $27,575 before its film rights were purchased by
Miramax Films and $230,000 was spent on music licensing and editing.

15
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
It was shot in the convenience and video stores where Smith worked in real life.

16
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
Clerks had its premiere at the Sundance Film Festival on January 22,
1994, and was released in the United States on October 19.

17
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
The film received positive reviews and grossed $4.4
million, launching Smith's career.

18
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
Often regarded as a landmark in independent filmmaking, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film
Registry by the Library of Congress in 2019 as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

19
01:19:27,272 --> 01:19:33,272
In 2006, a sequel was released, followed by a third installment in 2022.

20
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
The film explores themes of salesclerk, work, new jersey, gas station, loser.

21
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The tone is lighthearted.
